# Replit working artefacts (spreadsheets, pasted notes, screenshots uploaded for
# testing). Never part of the build; team members keep their own copies. Excluded so
# client-supplied data cannot land permanently in repo history.
# NOTE: this MUST be `attached_assets/*` (contents), not `attached_assets/` (the
# directory). Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the
# negations below would silently do nothing.
attached_assets/*

# ── EXCEPT the two files that ARE build inputs ──────────────────────────────
# The @assets alias (vite.config.ts) points at attached_assets/, so anything imported
# through it must stay tracked or `npm run build` fails with ENOENT. sfiLookup.ts also
# reads the component-tree CSV from disk at runtime.
# If you add a NEW import from @assets, add the file here too — or better, put it in
# client/src/assets/ so this list stops growing.
!attached_assets/SAIL logo Transparent_1753957135582.png
!attached_assets/component tree_1761646533252.csv
